  "summary": "Chapter 16 now contains the checked countable-pole construction and both full proofs. On every positive Hermitian background, a fixed stronger potential supplies stretching competitors and equality of ordinary and ideal envelopes below every continuous obstacle. The prescribed poles can be dense and all multiplier ideals remain trivial. The proof preserves the book definition using equality of multiplier ideals: the bounded unrestricted envelope itself is a competitor. The general S09 zero-obstacle implication remains open. Exact Demailly source credit is given in Chapter 34, and Chapter 33 and the catalogue record the restricted progress. Both covers show October 9, 2026; the 1758-page public release and homepage description are verified.",
